            <section id="compliance">
</section>

<!-- NAVIGATING INDIAN AND GLOBAL STANDARDS: COMPLIANCE FOR STARTUPS -->
<section class="section" id="navigating-indian-and-global-standards-compliance-for-startups">
  <h2>Navigating Indian and Global Standards: Compliance for Startups</h2>
  <p>Compliance is a moving target, especially for aerosol products which are subject to both chemical and pressure vessel regulations. In India, the Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS) provides guidelines like IS 13101 for aerosol containers. Globally, compliance with the UN Model Regulations for the Transport of Dangerous Goods is essential for any export activity. Understanding these frameworks early in the product development cycle saves startups from costly redesigns and legal hurdles.</p>
  <p>
                    Compliance is a moving target, especially for aerosol products which are subject to both chemical
                    and pressure vessel regulations. In India, the Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS) provides guidelines
                    like IS 13101 for aerosol containers. Globally, compliance with the UN Model Regulations for the
                    Transport of Dangerous Goods is essential for any export activity. Understanding these frameworks
                    early in the product development cycle saves startups from costly redesigns and legal hurdles.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Furthermore, environmental regulations are becoming stricter. The transition away from high-GWP
                    (Global Warming Potential) propellants like HFCs toward more sustainable options like LPG, DME, or
                    compressed gases (CO2, N2) must be reflected in all technical documentation. Startups that
                    proactively adopt green chemistry and document it correctly will find it easier to enter premium
                    markets in Europe and North America.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>ISO 9001:</strong> The gold standard for quality management systems.</li>
                    <li><strong>BIS (India):</strong> Crucial for domestic market entry and consumer trust. See <a
                            href="https://www.bis.gov.in/">Bureau of Indian
                            Standards</a> for technical specifications.</li>
                    <li><strong>GHS Compliance:</strong> Essential for international hazard communication.</li>
                    <li><strong>VOC Regulations:</strong> Monitoring volatile organic compounds to meet environmental
                        targets.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

